Step 1: Handle edge case.
    • If strs is null OR strs.length == 0:
      ○ Return empty string ""
Step 2: Use first string as reference.
    • Take strs[0] as base string
    • Compare all other strings with it character by character
Step 3: Traverse characters of first string.
    • For i = 0 to strs[0].length() − 1:
      ○ Get current character → ch = strs[0].charAt(i)
Step 4: Compare with all other strings.
    • For j = 1 to strs.length − 1:
      ○ Check two conditions:
        • If i == strs[j].length() (string ended)
        • OR strs[j].charAt(i) != ch (mismatch)
Step 5: Return prefix when mismatch found.
    • If any condition fails:
      ○ Return substring from 0 to i → strs[0].substring(0, i)
Step 6: If loop completes fully.
    • All characters matched for entire first string
    • Return strs[0]
Time Complexity Analysis:
    • Outer loop runs up to length of first string → O(n)
    • Inner loop runs for all strings → O(m)
    • Total comparisons → O(n × m)
    • Total Time Complexity → O(n × m)
      (Where n = length of smallest string, m = number of strings)
Space Complexity Analysis:
    • No extra data structures used
    • Only variables used → constant space
    • Total Space Complexity → O(1)



















